From: sbe1v1k 25.12-6.18 port <noreply@sbe1v1k-build>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-dp: index the RPS device flow table with hash_32 for 6.18

6.18 replaced the rps_dev_flow_table mask member with a u8 log (the table
now holds 1 << log entries and the core picks a slot with
hash_32(hash, log), see rfs_slot() in net/core/dev.c). nss_dp_main.c
still reads flow_table->mask:

  nss_dp_main.c:697:54: error: 'struct rps_dev_flow_table' has no member named 'mask'

Use the same hash_32() the core uses so the steering check keeps looking
at the slot the kernel will actually use. struct rps_sock_flow_table
still carries its mask, so the sock table access is unchanged.

Classification: portability (kernel API, same slot selection as core).
--- a/nss_dp_main.c
+++ b/nss_dp_main.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/hash.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/version.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
@@ -694,7 +695,7 @@
 	}
 
 	hash = skb_get_hash(skb);
-	rxflow = &flow_table->flows[hash & flow_table->mask];
+	rxflow = &flow_table->flows[hash_32(hash, flow_table->log)];
 	rxcpu = (uint32_t)rxflow->cpu;
 
 	sock_flow_table = rcu_dereference(net_hotdata.rps_sock_flow_table);
